            <ArticleTitle>Which of three structures is AZD-3199? WO-2008104790, WO-2008096112 and WO-2008096119.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1157-63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1517/13543770902815527</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>AstraZeneca progressed the long acting beta(2) agonist into Phase II studies for the treatment of asthma and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease in August 2008. These three applications claim specific salt forms of three different long acting beta(2) agonists, all benzothiazolone derivatives. It would seem that one claims AZD-3199 whereas the other two claim backup compounds.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
